course: dictionary
lesson: 13850
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The word jogger has two. The first meaning is a person who runs slowly and steadily for exercise. «The early-morning jogger waved as she passed the park gate.» Here the jogger is a person.
explain: The second meaning is about clothes. Joggers, in the plural, are soft, loose trousers with elastic at the ankles. «Put your joggers on for PE, please.» Here joggers are trousers, not people.
explain: How do you know which meaning to use? Read the words around it. Runners, park, morning and speed point to the person. Trousers, wear, PE and elastic point to clothes. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A jogger is a person who runs slowly and steadily for exercise.
fact: «Joggers» in the plural can mean soft, loose trousers with elastic at the ankles.
fact: Phrases to learn: an early-morning jogger, a pair of joggers.
fact: In maths problems, a jogger runs a distance at a steady speed, so you can work out how far they go.
exercise: «The early-morning jogger waved as she ran past the park gate.» What is a jogger in this sentence? | A gate that opens and closes | *A person who runs slowly and steadily for exercise | A bird that sings in the morning | A bus driver
exercise: «Put your joggers on for PE, please.» What are joggers here? | A small hill in the park | *Soft, loose trousers with elastic at the ankles | A type of football | Running shoes with spikes
exercise: Ravi says a jogger is always a person. Is he right? | No, it is always a car | Yes, it is always a bird | Yes, it is always a person | *No, joggers can also be soft, loose trousers
test: «A jogger runs at a steady speed of 6 km an hour.» How far does she run in 2 hours? | 8 km | *12 km | 4 km | 18 km
test: «He wore his joggers to the gym.» What does joggers most likely mean here? | *Soft, loose trousers | A runner | A pair of running shoes | A bench in the park
exam: In the phrase «a pair of joggers», what does joggers mean? | *Soft, loose trousers with elastic at the ankles | A steady speed | Park gates | Early-morning runners
